35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, most of our costs are fixed regardless of attendance! Also, a lot of people struggle to pay the full renewal all at once.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,It seems that charging per event can be dangerous. I've found that turnout dropped significantly when we introduced door charges.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"It's exactly as I thought. A tiny group does all the work and attends everything, while eighteen people didn't show up once!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The administrative cost of collecting small fees is immense. Chasing individual payments takes six times longer than a single annual collection.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"A lot of potential members are scared off by a big upfront annual fee, and even current members are struggling to pay it.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"If seventy percent is fixed, we can't just charge per activity, or we'll go broke. But we can't ignore that people struggle with the lump sum.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Takumi, the imbalance is clear, but we must be careful. If we make it too transactional, people stop feeling like they belong.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Takumi,,But is it fair that the same nine people do all the setup and pay the same as someone who never shows up?,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, fairness is one thing, but efficiency is another. Calculating part-year fees for mid-year joiners is a nightmare for the treasurer.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,Maybe there's a middle ground? We need to keep it welcoming for newcomers but not kill the treasurer.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Kenji, what if we had different levels? That might help the people who can't pay all at once or don't come often.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,I worry that tiers might create a social divide. We want people to feel equal when they walk through the door.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Takumi,,I'd rather have tiers than a flat fee that rewards people for doing nothing. The regulars deserve a better deal.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Toshio,,Any system that requires monthly chasing or custom calculations for every new member is a failure. Simplicity is key for the books.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"I'm worried that if we make it too visible who is paying what, the ""drift in"" feeling will disappear.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,"We have to balance the fixed costs, the treasurer's sanity, and the members' wallets. This is trickier than I thought!","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,Let us consider the options carefully. We must protect the spirit of the club while ensuring its survival.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"As long as the people doing the work aren't the only ones paying for the ghosts, I'm open to suggestions.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I will support whatever option minimizes the manual labor for the treasurer.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,I just want a system that doesn't scare away the people who are still deciding if they fit in.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
