60,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Option A is simple, but we know people struggle with the lump sum. Option B might be a good compromise for the costs.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,Option C is out for me. We've already seen that charging per event makes people hesitate to attend.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Takumi,,Option B is the only one that addresses the unfairness. Why should the regulars subsidize the people who never show up?,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Option A is the most efficient for the treasurer. Option C is a disaster. Option B is acceptable if the tiers are fixed.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Option A is too high a barrier for new people. Option C is welcoming, but @Jonathan is right about the atmosphere.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Kenji, would Option B feel too restrictive? Or would it be easier than a big flat fee?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"I fear Option B will lead to ""grades"" of members, which creates a psychological barrier. Option A preserves the sense of unity.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"Unity is just a word for ""the regulars pay for everyone else."" I'm voting for B.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, as long as B doesn't involve chasing small payments every week, it's viable. But A is still the cleanest.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Kenji,,I think B is better than A because it gives people a way to start small without the pressure of a full year.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mio,,I'm leaning towards B. It helps with the fixed costs but acknowledges that not everyone uses the club the same way.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I still prefer A. It's the only way to ensure that coming to a meeting is a given, not a decision.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Takumi,,I can't support A. It's fundamentally unfair to the people who actually run the place.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Toshio,,I'll go with A. The treasurer's time is too valuable to spend on managing tiers and calculations.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'll go with B. It's the best way to keep the door open for newcomers while staying sustainable.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Mio,,It looks like we're split. I'll stick with B to help those who can't afford the full flat fee.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I will maintain my vote for A. The social health of the club is more important than perfect accounting.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Takumi,,B is the only fair choice.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Toshio,,A is the only professional choice.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Kenji,,B is the most welcoming choice.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
